div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Four days earlier, " [:a {:href "/athletes/126517"} "Lee Kiefer"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/151977"} "Lauren Scruggs"] " had won gold and silver in the individual foil, and they would lead the USA team. They were only seeded #2 as Italy was very strong, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505325"} "Martina Favaretto"] " (2), " [:a {:href "/athletes/144048"} "Alice Volpi"] " (3), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/123944"} "Arianna Errigo"] " (4) world ranking only behind Kiefer individually. Italy had won four of the last six titles in this event, winning in 1996-2004 and 2012."] "\n\n" [:p {} "As expected, Italy and the United States won their first two matches and met in the final. In the last two bouts, Volpi defeated Kiefer 6-5 and Errigo took down Scruggs, 7-6, but to no avail, as the Americans by then had built up too big a lead and won the gold medal, 45-39. France was the third seed but lost to Canada in the first round. Canada met Japan for the bronze medal. After eight bouts, Japan led 32-29. In the final bout, Canada had the individual gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/129452"} "Eleanor Harvey"] ", who met " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505365"} "Yuka Ueno"] ", and she won 3-1, but it was not enough to pull out the victory, as Japan took the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/126517"} "Lee Kiefer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/151977"} "Lauren Scruggs"] " • " [:a {:href "/at